<p class="page-title">Profile</p>
<p class="profile-venue-name" id="profile-venue-name"></p>

{# No switcher here (restaurant switching is /menu/-only — see
   venue-header.njk) — just enough data for profile.js to resolve an id
   to a display name, since it can't read that off a sidemenu switcher
   DOM (removed, see nav.njk). #}
<ul id="profile-restaurant-names" hidden>
  {% for restaurant in restaurants %}
  <li data-restaurant-id="{{ restaurant.id }}">{{ restaurant.name }}</li>
  {% endfor %}
</ul>

{# Progress lives here now, not on its own /stats/ page — it's the same
   shareable-with-management data Profile itself is for, not a separate
   destination. Reset stays here too, as the full original widget
   (name + tier + Reset together) — it's a real, if occasional,
   management action (re-training someone), not just a private debug
   tool, so it belongs on the shareable page rather than tucked away on
   /settings/. #}
<h2 class="profile-section-title">Progress</h2>
<div class="profile-sections" id="profile-sections">
  <p>Loading…</p>
</div>
